===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|en|enm|doke}}, {{m|enm|ducke}}, {{m|enm|dukke}}, {{m|enm|dokke}}, {{m|enm|douke}}, {{m|enm|duke}}, from {{inh|en|ang|duce}}, {{m|ang|dūce||duck|lit=dipper, diver, ducker}}, from {{der|en|ang|*dūcan||to dip, dive, duck}}, from {{der|en|gmw-pro|*dūkan}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*dūkaną||to dive, bend down}}. See verb above.

{{rel-top|Cognates}}
Cognate with {{cog|sco|duik}}, {{m|sco|duke}}, {{m|sco|dook||duck}}, {{cog|da|dukand}}, {{m|da|dykand||sea-duck}}, {{cog|sv|dykfågel||a diver, diving bird, plungeon}}, {{cog|nl|duiker|t=diver, dipper, plunger}}, {{cog|nds-de|Düker|t=diver}}, {{cog|de|Taucher|t=diver, plunger}}. {{rel-bottom}}

For the meaning development compare with {{m+|ru|ныро́к||[[pochard]]}} connected with {{m|ru|ныря́ть||to dive}}.

